qemu-11.0.3-macos-gl.patch

Teaches QEMU's Cocoa display to render through OpenGL on macOS, which is what
makes the virtio-gpu-gl device usable and gives guests hardware-accelerated
graphics via ANGLE and Metal.

Derived from Akihiko Odaki's macOS virgl work, by way of the patch carried in
https://github.com/startergo/homebrew-qemu-virgl-kosmickrisp, rebased onto the
QEMU 11.0.3 release. Upstream QEMU has not merged this work.

Rebasing notes: the upstream patch also carries CoreAudio changes, SDL support
and an EGL refactor. None are needed here — march uses the Cocoa display and
does not rely on QEMU for audio — and none applied cleanly to 11.0.3, so this
patch contains only the hunks that did: the OpenGL display plumbing.

QEMU is GPL-2.0-only; this patch inherits that licence.
